From abf4ff5a6fdc7cc80301979f11f5e1e8e93d0972 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.local>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 07:57:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Launch readiness: honest numbers, legal pages, OG fallback,
 PWA
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

FABRICATED STATISTICS REMOVED — the most important item here.
The homepage advertised '500+ Families Served', '200+ Livestreams',
'1K+ QR Codes' and '50+ Partner Parlours'. MemoryGlen has not launched.
Every one of those numbers was untrue, on a product whose entire value is
being trustworthy with a family's memories, and on a page investors read.
Replaced with what is true today. Put real numbers back when they are
real.

MEMORIAL ORDERING — John Peters now leads the directory as the public
demo; Virginia sits beneath him and keeps her quiet Founding Memorial
badge.

OPEN GRAPH — dataset memorials shared with the homepage hero as their
preview image, so a memorial unfurled in WhatsApp showed a picture of a
landing page. Now uses the person's own portrait where one exists and a
dignified neutral 1200x630 card otherwise. Never the homepage hero.

LEGAL — Terms of Service and Privacy Policy, plain language, with footer
links on every page. Covers content ownership, family control of
memorials, and a real section on living people who appear in family
trees: they can ask to be removed, without a reason and without the
family owner's agreement. POPIA and GDPR named.
⚠️ NOT reviewed by a lawyer. Placeholders for the registered entity and
the POPIA Information Officer are marked in legalContent.ts.

PWA — manifest.webmanifest with 192, 512 and maskable icons, standalone
display, brand theme colour; a conservative service worker; and an
offline shell. Navigations are network-first on purpose: showing someone
a stale copy of their mother's memorial, or one since made private,
would be worse than showing nothing. Account and sign-in are never
cached.

14 tests. 61 pass in total.
